        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test demonstrate air leakage on the following house components:

-	Window: Air leakage has been observed on the window located in the dining room, on the lower left corner. We recommend to fill the space between the window unit and the wall with caulking. This might reduce the air leakage.

-	Door: We noticed air leakage around the back door knob. The addition of weather stripping might reduce the leakage and increase the air tightness of the door.

-	Receptacles: At the moment of the infiltration test, we noticed leakage from the receptacles. We recommend the installation of insulation custom made for electrical boxes.

-	Bathroom fans: We noticed air leakage from the exhausting fans. This problem is a unit issue. There is nothing much to do except the replacement of the unit itself. 

-	Mechanical equipment chimneys: We noticed air leakage from the wood stove and boiler chimney. This situation is normal.



Overall, the infiltration test result showed that the house has a fairly good air tightness.  

</airSeal>
                <ceilings>At the time of the inspection we observed that the roof insulation level is R-40. We recommend adding insulation to meet the actual standard based at R-60.</ceilings>
                <foundation>At the time of the inspection we observed some sections of the foundation wall who are not insulated. We recommend the addition of insulation to reach a minimum of R-10. We recommend the use of rigid foam for the following reasons:

-Reduction of the thermal bridge

-Insulate and act also as a vapour barrier.

</foundation>
                <VentilationSystem>Following the infiltration test, the natural ventilation in the house is not enough. The house showed signs of a high level of humidity. Mould has been observed, on the main floor, on the walls and ceiling. Mechanical ventilation is recommended to compensate for the lack of ventilation and control the humidity inside the house.

We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) unit, ENERGY STAR and HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) certified.

We also recommend and recommend the installation of an hygrometer to monitor the level of humidity inside the house. The percentage of humidity should be between 30-50% in winter and 40-60% in summer.

</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
            <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="" />
        </Options>
